1. ABOUT THIS POLICY
Bida Reels provides short-drama and reels viewing features. This policy explains
how account information, app activity, device information, and other data are
handled when you use the app. It also describes services used for sign-in,
advertising and content delivery, and notes the planned VIP purchase feature.

2. ACCOUNT INFORMATION
When you sign in with Google, the app uses Google Sign-In and Firebase
Authentication. The app stores your Firebase user ID, Google display name,
email address, profile-photo URL, and account/login timestamps in Firebase
Realtime Database. This information supports account access and administration.
The app does not receive or store your Google account password.
Account records may also include blocked status, VIP status, and VIP or
ad-free entitlement expiration dates.

3. DEVICE AND SESSION INFORMATION
For active VIP-session management, the app stores a session identifier,
a device identifier, device name, and session timestamp. The current app
constructs its device identifier from a hash of the app package and Android ID,
or uses a generated identifier when Android ID is unavailable. This information
is used to recognize an active device/session and manage VIP access.

4. APP ACTIVITY AND LOCAL STORAGE
The app stores settings such as selected provider, search history, favorites,
viewing progress, and cached content/images on the device. Nickname changes
and profile images selected through the app's profile editor are stored locally;
they are separate from the Google profile information stored for your account.
Search terms and content requests may be sent to the selected content provider
or hosting service to retrieve results and deliver videos or images.
For signed-in users, episode-unlock records are also stored in Firebase.
These records contain a drama/series identifier, unlocked episode limit,
update timestamp, and access-expiration timestamp.
Expiration of episode access does not itself mean deletion of the server record.

5. ADVERTISING
Bida Reels uses Google AdMob / Google Mobile Ads SDK for rewarded and
interstitial advertising. Ad requests can begin during app startup/Splash,
including while the login screen is visible, when ads are enabled.
The SDK handles data such as IP address, device/account identifiers,
ad interactions, and diagnostic information for advertising, analytics,
and fraud prevention. An IP address may be used to estimate general location.
Advertising identifiers and ad handling may vary with device settings,
SDK configuration, and applicable consent choices.
Rewarded ads can be used to unlock episodes. Ad-free/VIP access changes
ad-display behavior but does not remove account management.
Google privacy policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy
AdMob disclosure: https://developers.google.com/admob/android/privacy/play-data-disclosure

6. VIP IN-APP PURCHASES — PLANNED
We plan to introduce VIP in-app purchases in an upcoming update. This purchase
feature is not currently available in the app. Before it becomes available,
we will update this policy to explain the billing service used, information
handled for purchase verification and VIP access, and related retention and
deletion practices. Existing VIP entitlements may still be managed through
account administration; they are separate from the planned purchase feature.

7. SERVICE PROVIDERS AND SHARING
Google/Firebase supports authentication, account storage, and advertising.
Content APIs, image/video hosts, and external websites receive
the network requests needed to deliver their services, which can include

IP address and requested resources. Opening an update link transfers you
to an external browser or app store.
Authorized administrators may access account records to provide support,
manage VIP entitlements, enforce access restrictions, and process requests.
We do not sell or rent your personal information. Information may be handled
by service providers to operate the app or disclosed where legally required.

8. SECURITY
The app uses HTTPS for Firebase and ad services. We use reasonable security measures appropriate to the services
we operate. No storage or transmission method can guarantee complete security.

